# chat-45: config zs = M1-B + COH + SB1 (SB1 is schedule-only, bitwise equal to M1-B + COH), 45 GB line, C 256. Lossy (QOM on the chat and code sets, QOM-gated MTP drafts).
# Source: BigMoE data/stack/chat_env.txt + R57_SB1=1 (== pfd.sh ZS); runs pdz0. Gate status: README, Configs.
# PF-D on (R57_PFD=1,R57_PFD_V=4,R57_PFD_AHEAD=1; BigMoE rel0 aa1ca3b, pfd.sh arm pdz4a, WED_TESTS Mon 00:09): first token from
# pool-resident experts, tokens bitwise equal to zs without it (12/12 IFEval, logits hash 721/721); lifetime peak +1.3 GB.
# 1.2.1: + P2 (LOSSY, gated): R57_P2=256,R57_P2_ROWS=16,R57_P2_VERIFY=0. A prompt of 256 tokens or fewer skips the prefill and
# runs as 16-row plain forwards on the decode's check path; longer prompts take the prefill above (PF-D) unchanged. On the 12
# IFEval prompts (BigMoE's 45 GB first-token A/B, Fri 13 Nov 02:16, bb61289) the first token took 0.47 s (median) instead of
# 2.44 s, the lifetime peak 42.3-42.4 vs 43.6-43.7 GB; such a prompt's answer differs from the prefill path's (2 of 12 equal).
# EvalSuite's 45 GB P2 gate (Fri 13 Nov, f25a578; PREREG_p2gate45 + amendments 1, 1a, 1b) found the scores the same: IFBench
# +2.00 pt (p 0.68), GPQA Diamond's 67 prompts of <= 256 tokens -1.49 pt (p 1.00), 5 longer-prompt controls token-identical.
# The env line below = BigMoE data/stack/chat45_p2_env.txt line 2 (blob e4012e80) verbatim, the gate's P2 arm: 1.2.0's
# settings with R57_QOM_SETS widened to lcb6, ifbench and gpqad as the gate ran them (a chat prompt's set, multi, is a QOM
# set in both), plus the three P2 keys.
# Decode loop: engine/loop/r57_screen_c45p2.py (BigMoE 3bf3dbd, snapshot c45p2) = the gate's loop (P3 snapshot c477b60,
# r57_screen_p3.py, sha256 e410133cfe69) with its 19 frozen-tree paths renamed for the package's path rewrite: rel1's loop +
# P2 v0 and its runs.json field; with R57_P2 unset it runs as rel1's. Its sibling modules are rel1's (1.2.0's), so pflm.py
# is 1.2.0's: the gate ran P3's copy, which adds P3's fold (R57_PFD_FOLD, unset in the gate and here) and refactors the
# read-ahead around it. 1.2.1's release checks compare the tokens with 1.2.0's chat-45 on a prompt well over 256 tokens and
# with the gate's own rows on the first 5 keys of its P2 arm.
# Memory: LIMITS.md (P2 lowers the short prompts' peak; long prompts can pass the 45 GB line).
SNAPSHOT=c45p2
C=256
BIGMOE_EXT_BUILD=build_qom,R57_REFTOK=,R57_FAST=QOM,R57_D17=1,R57_D7B=code,R57_HC8=1,REF2_HC8_FAST=1,R57_DNR=1,R57_HCB=1,REF2_SMALL_NATIVE=1,R57_D7BNAX=1,REF2_OOO_1C=1,R57_NAX=1,REF2_NAX_1CQ=1,REF2_DN_KS=1,REF2_GDN_LAZY=1,D7BNAX_32=2,R57_FASTTAX=1,R57_SBN=2,R57_DSUB=1,R57_SVH=1,R57_RELAX_SPAN=1,R57_RELAX_SPAN_RULE=R2:2:0.25,R57_COPY=g2,REF2_KEEP_CACHES=1,R57_WIRED=1,BIGMOE_PAUSE_EVERY_MS=50,R57_S0CARRY=1,REF2_SB_FIRST=1,REF2_PLE_LATE=1,REF2_COMMIT_SUB=9,R57_DQ1=1,R57_QOM_MTP=2,REF2_NAX_COH=1,R57_SB1=1,R57_PFD=1,R57_PFD_V=4,R57_PFD_AHEAD=1,R57_P2=256,R57_P2_ROWS=16,R57_P2_VERIFY=0,R57_QOM_SETS=humaneval,mbpp,ifeval,multi,lcb6,ifbench,gpqad
